  "kind": "philosophical",
  "epistemic_status": "hypothesized",
  "title": "Each occasion is partly self-determining",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "d20dc3ef-ae92-41c6-87b1-9c9380c7a6a6",
      "text": "Causation includes both determination by the antecedent world, the efficient causation of past occasions, and self-determination, the final causation of the occasion in its becoming. Actuality is the decision amid potentiality: the past conditions how an occasion takes it into account but does not fully determine it. Self-determination gives rise to probabilistic laws and to human freedom.",
